examples.question_text:
$PT$ is tangent to a circle with centre $O$ at $T$. Given $\angle TOP=63^{\circ}$, find $x=\angle OPT$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (T) at (0,1.5);\coordinate (P) at (2.944,1.5);
\draw (O) circle (1.5);\draw (O)--(T)--(P)--cycle;
\draw (0,1.3)--(0.2,1.3)--(0.2,1.5);
\fill (O) circle (1pt);
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};\node[above] at (T) {$T$};\node[right] at (P) {$P$};
\node at (0.35,0.65) {$63^{\circ}$};\node at (2.2,1.3) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$PT$ and $PQ$ are tangents to a circle with centre $O$. The smaller angle $\angle TOQ=120^{\circ}$. Find (a) $\angle TPQ$, (b) $\angle PTQ$, and (c) $\angle TCQ$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (4,0);\coordinate (T) at (1,1.73205);\coordinate (Q) at (1,-1.73205);\coordinate (C) at (-2,0);
\draw (O) circle (2);\draw (P)--(T)--(Q)--(P);\draw (T)--(O)--(Q);\draw (T)--(C)--(Q);
\fill (O) circle (1pt);
\node[left] at (O) {$O$};\node[right] at (P) {$P$};\node[above] at (T) {$T$};\node[below] at (Q) {$Q$};\node[left] at (C) {$C$};
\node at (0.65,0) {$120^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$XY$ is tangent to the circle at $T$. Given $\angle ATB=45^{\circ}$ and $\angle BTY=70^{\circ}$, find (a) $\angle TAB$, (b) $\angle ABT$, and (c) $\angle XTA$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (T) at (0,-2);\coordinate (A) at (-1.532089,1.285575);\coordinate (B) at (1.28558,1.53209);
\draw (0,0) circle (2);\draw (-2.8,-2)--(2.8,-2);\draw (T)--(A)--(B)--cycle;
\node[below] at (T) {$T$};\node[left] at (A) {$A$};\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};\node[below] at (-2.8,-2) {$X$};\node[below] at (2.8,-2) {$Y$};
\node at (-0.12,-1.25) {$45^{\circ}$};\node at (0.9,-1.65) {$70^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$PC$ and $PQ$ are tangents to a circle with centre $O$. Secant $PNB$ passes through $O$, meeting the circle first at $N$. Given $PN=2\text{ cm}$, $NB=6\text{ cm}$, $OP=5\text{ cm}$ and $\angle NCP\approx26.57^{\circ}$, find (a) $PC$, (b) $PQ$, (c) the radius $OC$, and (d) $y=\angle NBC$ to 2 decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},scale=0.65]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (5,0);\coordinate (C) at (1.8,2.4);\coordinate (Q) at (1.8,-2.4);\coordinate (N) at (3,0);\coordinate (B) at (-3,0);
\draw (O) circle (3);\draw (P)--(C)--(N);\draw (P)--(Q);\draw (P)--(B)--(C);\draw (O)--(C);
\fill (O) circle (1pt);
\node[above left,xshift=-3pt,yshift=3pt] at (O) {$O$};\node[right] at (P) {$P$};\node[above] at (C) {$C$};\node[below] at (Q) {$Q$};\node[below right] at (N) {$N$};\node[left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (4,0) {$2\text{ cm}$};\node[below,yshift=-12pt] at (-1.3,0) {$NB=6\text{ cm}$};\node at (-1.85,0.3) {$y$};
\node[above right] at (2.5,2) {$26.57^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$PC$ is tangent to a circle at $C$. A secant from $P$ meets the circle first at $N$ and then at $B$. Given $PC=14\text{ cm}$ and $PN=7\text{ cm}$, find $NB$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},scale=0.75]
\coordinate (P) at (3.5,0);\coordinate (N) at (2.1,0);\coordinate (B) at (-2.1,0);\coordinate (C) at (1.26,1.68);
\draw (0,0) circle (2.1);\draw (P)--(B);\draw (P)--(C);
\node[right] at (P) {$P$};\node[below] at (N) {$N$};\node[left] at (B) {$B$};\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (2.8,0) {$7\text{ cm}$};\node[above right] at (2.38,0.84) {$14\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$PC$ is tangent to a circle at $C$. A secant from $P$ meets the circle first at $N$ and then at $B$. Given $PN=5\text{ cm}$ and $NB=9\text{ cm}$, find the exact length of $PC$ in surd form.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (P) at (3.16667,0);\coordinate (N) at (1.5,0);\coordinate (B) at (-1.5,0);\coordinate (C) at (0.710526,1.320964);
\draw (0,0) circle (1.5);\draw (P)--(B);\draw (P)--(C);
\node[right] at (P) {$P$};\node[below] at (N) {$N$};\node[left] at (B) {$B$};\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (2.3333,0) {$5\text{ cm}$};\node[below] at (0,0) {$9\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$PT$ and $PQ$ are tangents to a circle. Given $\angle TPQ=48^{\circ}$, $PT=15\text{ cm}$ and $PA=10\text{ cm}$, find (a) $x=\angle PTQ$ and (b) the full secant length $PB$. The secant meets the circle first at $A$ and then at $B$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (4.91719,0);\coordinate (T) at (0.81347,1.82709);\coordinate (Q) at (0.81347,-1.82709);\coordinate (A) at (1.953394,0.429247);\coordinate (B) at (-1.751348,0.965806);
\draw (O) circle (2);\draw (P)--(T)--(Q)--(P);\draw (P)--(B);
\node[right] at (P) {$P$};\node[above] at (T) {$T$};\node[below] at (Q) {$Q$};\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};\node[above left] at (B) {$B$};
\draw (P) ++(156:0.75) arc[start angle=156,end angle=204,radius=0.75];
\node (fullanglelabel) at (3.7,-0.85) {$48^{\circ}$};
\draw (fullanglelabel.north east)--(4.18358,-0.15593);
\node at (0.98,1.25) {$x$};\node[above right] at (2.7,1.05) {$15\text{ cm}$};\node[below] at (3.3,0.25) {$10\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$PA$ and $PB$ are tangents from an external point $P$ to a circle with centre $O$. (a) Prove that $\triangle PAO\equiv\triangle PBO$. (b) Hence prove that $PA=PB$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (4,0);\coordinate (A) at (1,1.73205);\coordinate (B) at (1,-1.73205);
\draw (O) circle (2);\draw (O)--(A)--(P)--(B)--(O);\draw (O)--(P);
\fill (O) circle (1pt);
\node[left] at (O) {$O$};\node[right] at (P) {$P$};\node[above] at (A) {$A$};\node[below] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
